ITEM 15 -- the wide-binary ORIENTATION split: does the boost know which way the Galaxy is?
====================================================================================================================
  El-Badry+2021 Gaia EDR3 catalogue: 1817594 pairs loaded
  clean sample (R_chance_align < 0.01, RUWE < 1.4 both, d < 250 pc, parallax S/N > 50 both, 4 < M_G < 11 both, |dmu|/sigma > 5): 39702 pairs
  with a well-defined sky orientation: 39702 pairs; <cos^2 phi> about the Galactic-centre axis = 0.4894 (isotropic value 0.5)
  [PASS] 15-isotropy the SKY COVERAGE itself is close to isotropic about the Galactic-centre axis, so the split below is not dominated by one hemisphere of the survey.  (Wide pairs are found preferentially at high Galactic latitude where crowding is low, which tilts <cos^2 phi> slightly; the size of that tilt is the number quoted)   (<cos^2 phi>_GC = 0.4894, <cos^2 phi>_ecliptic-pole = 0.5099, isotropic = 0.5000)

